# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*
!.env.example

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

/src/generated/prisma

# Playwright
/playwright-report/
/test-results/
/.playwright-cli/

# Agent tooling — machine-local and regenerable, so it is deliberately not committed.
#
# `.claude/skills/*` are SYMLINKS into `.agents/skills/`. Git on Windows checks
# symlinks out as plain text files containing the link target, so committing
# them hands every collaborator a set of broken paths pointing at a directory
# that only exists on this machine.
#
# Restore locally with `npx prisma init` (re-installs the Prisma skill set) —
# see SETUP.md. Nothing in the application reads these.
/.agents/
/.claude/
/.windsurf/
/skills-lock.json

# Graphify's analysis cache — a few megabytes of JSON derived entirely from the
# source tree beside it. Committing it would put a second, staler copy of the
# codebase in the repo and produce an enormous diff on every run.
/graphify-out/

.vercel
.env*
